From 684fa5da3233f950130f2151b82fd7be365730cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ingmar Steen <iksteen@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 21:24:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] matroskademux: accept a large element the file vouches
 for

MAX_BLOCK_SIZE refuses any element over 32 MiB, and in streaming mode
that refusal is fatal:

  reading large block of size 35821506 not supported; file might be corrupt

The size is not evidence of corruption on its own. Fansubbed releases
attach their subtitle fonts, and a CJK font pack passes 32 MiB without
being remarkable - 12 of 1108 Matroska files in one ordinary library
carry Attachments over the limit, and another 28 sit between 8 and 32
MiB, so the boundary is one releases approach routinely rather than a
frontier only broken files reach. Every one of those 12 is undemuxable
in streaming mode while pull mode plays it, because pull can skip what
it cannot hold and streaming cannot.

What does distinguish a corrupt size is whether the element could be
there at all. Upstream usually knows the length, and the demuxer
already consults it for SeekHead validation, so when the element ends
inside the file the size is corroborated by the file itself. Accept
that case, bounded by MAX_SANE_ELEMENT_SIZE so the adapter still has a
ceiling, and leave everything else - unknown length, or an element
running past the end - refused exactly as before.

Measured on 1.28.5 with the same change, through a push-only appsrc so
pull cannot be reached: the file demuxes, and the demuxer publishes all
45 attachments instead of dying. A file in the same library claiming a
128041197 byte element inside 88.8 MB still fails, which is the case
this guard was written for and which ffmpeg independently reports as
"exceeds containing master element".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011KQFNXanCWf4EjotC8Ah4z
---
 .../gst/matroska/matroska-demux.c             | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/subprojects/gst-plugins-good/gst/matroska/matroska-demux.c b/subprojects/gst-plugins-good/gst/matroska/matroska-demux.c
index 14188913..de3b6057 100644
--- a/subprojects/gst-plugins-good/gst/matroska/matroska-demux.c
+++ b/subprojects/gst-plugins-good/gst/matroska/matroska-demux.c
@@ -6089,11 +6089,35 @@ gst_matroska_demux_parse_contents (GstMatroskaDemux * demux, GstEbmlRead * ebml)
 #define GST_FLOW_OVERFLOW   GST_FLOW_CUSTOM_ERROR
 
 #define MAX_BLOCK_SIZE (32 * 1024 * 1024)
+/* Ceiling for an element we accept on the strength of it fitting inside
+ * the file. Generous enough for the font packs fansubbed releases
+ * attach (tens of MB is routine), small enough to bound what streaming
+ * has to hold in the adapter. */
+#define MAX_SANE_ELEMENT_SIZE (256 * 1024 * 1024)
 
 static inline GstFlowReturn
 gst_matroska_demux_check_read_size (GstMatroskaDemux * demux, guint64 bytes)
 {
   if (G_UNLIKELY (bytes > MAX_BLOCK_SIZE)) {
+    /* A large element is only suspicious if it could not possibly be
+     * there. When upstream knows the length and the element fits inside
+     * it, the size is corroborated by the file itself and the element is
+     * real data - Attachments carrying subtitle fonts run well past
+     * MAX_BLOCK_SIZE in ordinary releases, and refusing them makes such
+     * a file undemuxable in streaming mode while pull mode plays it. A
+     * declared size that runs past the end of the file is the corrupt
+     * case this guard is for, and stays refused. */
+    if (bytes <= MAX_SANE_ELEMENT_SIZE) {
+      gint64 length = gst_matroska_read_common_get_length (&demux->common);
+
+      if (length > 0 && demux->common.offset + bytes <= (guint64) length) {
+        GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (demux,
+            "accepting large element of size %" G_GUINT64_FORMAT
+            "; it fits within the %" G_GINT64_FORMAT " byte file", bytes,
+            length);
+        return GST_FLOW_OK;
+      }
+    }
     /* only a few blocks are expected/allowed to be large,
      * and will be recursed into, whereas others will be read and must fit */
     if (demux->streaming) {
